# PHASE 14 — MULTI-CURRENCY & FOREIGN EXCHANGE ACCOUNTING

## 1. PHASE OBJECTIVE

Implement the Accounting Web App's **Multi-Currency & Foreign Exchange
Accounting** capability on top of the existing accounting architecture.

The implementation must make the system capable of handling transactions
denominated in currencies other than the company's base currency while
preserving:

- exact double-entry accounting;
- immutable posted financial history;
- company isolation;
- fiscal-period controls;
- tax snapshots;
- existing document/accounting integrations;
- correct foreign-currency and base-currency values;
- historical exchange-rate integrity;
- realized and unrealized FX handling where supported;
- existing reporting architecture;
- existing audit and accounting-control infrastructure.

This phase must extend the existing accounting engine.

**DO NOT create a second accounting engine.**

The existing journal/posting/ledger architecture remains the single source of
accounting truth.

