# 4. HARD STOP CONDITIONS

STOP and report a design conflict before implementing if:

1. Existing currency fields have contradictory meanings.
2. Existing journal lines cannot distinguish transaction currency from base
   currency safely.
3. Existing posted journals would need historical values rewritten.
4. Existing reports depend on ambiguous currency values.
5. Existing tax snapshots cannot preserve the currency/rate context required for
   historical correctness.
6. A second accounting balance/source-of-truth would be required.
7. Existing company base-currency rules conflict with the proposed design.
8. A migration would require destructive rewriting of posted financial history.
9. Existing fixed-asset accounting cannot preserve historical currency values
   safely.
10. Multi-company isolation cannot be guaranteed.
11. Existing audit/control infrastructure cannot record important currency
    configuration/rate changes.
12. A global model observer is required merely to make the feature work safely.
13. The implementation would require changing already-posted journal amounts.
14. Existing report semantics would become ambiguous between transaction
    currency and base currency.

Do not work around a hard stop silently.

