# 19. UNREALIZED FX

Determine whether unrealized FX revaluation can be implemented safely using the
existing architecture.

If implemented:

- it must be a controlled accounting operation;
- it must operate against open foreign-currency monetary balances;
- it must create normal journal entries;
- it must respect fiscal periods;
- it must be auditable;
- it must not rewrite original transaction history;
- it must not permanently overwrite original transaction rates;
- reversal/revaluation cycles must be traceable.

If the current architecture cannot support this safely, **defer unrealized FX
revaluation** rather than creating an unsafe implementation.

Document the reason in the Phase 14 report.

